# Import TYPE aliasing used inside a `Box`-WRAPPING container type — here a
# function type `Callable[DT(...)]`, whose return position the type-axis
# rewrite must rename `DT` -> `DateTime` inside. This is the part of the
# rewrite the SELF-HOST currently DEFERS: the `TFunction` (and `TArray` /
# `TSlice`) recursion arms of `rename_aliases_type` reconstruct a
# `Box[SpannedType]` for the inner `Type`, and porting THAT trips a Rust-`gg`
# BIR-lowering bug (a self-recursive fn that pattern-matches on the `Type`
# enum AND reconstructs a `Box`-wrapped `Type` value mis-resolves the
# reconstructed `EnumInit` struct-id to a builtin in a large multi-module
# build; `field index N out of range for CRuntimeType` — pressure-dependent,
# does NOT repro standalone).
#
# The `TNamed`-generic-args arm IS restored (see `import_type_alias_nested`,
# which runs `2000`); only the `Box`-wrapping arms remain deferred. Rust `gg`
# handles THIS fixture correctly today, so the expected output below is the
# CORRECT language behavior — the self-host must reach it once the BIR
# struct-id collision is fixed and the `TFunction`/`TArray`/`TSlice` recursion
# arms are restored in `self_host_typechecker/meta.gg::rename_aliases_type`.
#
# Wired #[ignore] in tests/integration.rs because the SELF-HOST can't build it
# yet (the deferred Box-wrapping recursion); un-ignore when restored.

from std.datetime import DateTime as DT

# `DT` nested inside a function type's RETURN position (`TFunction` -> Box).
DT apply_stamp(Callable[DT(int)] f, int year):
    return f(year)

DT make_year(int year):
    return DT(year, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0)

void main():
    DT d = apply_stamp(make_year, 2000)
    print(f"{d.dt_year}")
